Upgrade to Nette 4
******************

{{maintitle: Upgrade to Nette 4 Automatically}}
{{description: Upgrade to nette/utils 4 and the other Nette 4 libraries: what DressCode rewrites, what it reports, and how to measure, plan and run the upgrade step by step.}}

.[perex]
Nette 4 is the set of libraries that moved to a new major version: `nette/utils` 4, `nette/php-generator` 4, `nette/mail` 4 and `nette/robot-loader` 4. Constants got new names, flags became named arguments, and a few methods disappeared. With the package `dresscode/upgrade-nette`, DressCode rewrites what can be rewritten and, for the rest, says what to write instead.


What It Looks Like
==================

An application on Nette 3 wants to move to `nette/utils` 4.0. The estimate tells how much work that is before anything changes:

/--pre .[terminal]
DRESS|CODE 1.3.0
Config     /var/www/shop/dresscode.neon
Upgrade    nette/utils 4.0 over 3 files

Must change, 2 topics with 12 findings
  nette/utils  10 findings in 3 files    needs ^4.0, automatic
  nette/utils  2 findings in 1 file      works on ^3.2, automatic
\--

Once `nette/utils` is raised to `^4.0`, DressCode rewrites the code by itself:

```php .[before]
$image->resize(300, 200, Image::FIT | Image::SHRINK_ONLY);
file_put_contents($this->file, Json::encode($products, Json::PRETTY));
return Strings::startsWith($code, 'sale-');
```

```php .[after]
$image->resize(300, 200, Image::OrSmaller | Image::ShrinkOnly);
file_put_contents($this->file, Json::encode($products, pretty: true));
return \str_starts_with($code, 'sale-');
```

It rewrites a method call only where the types from PHPStan say the method belongs to that class, and in the style the code of the project has. [Step by Step |#Step by Step] shows how to get there.


What Gets Rewritten
===================

The tables show samples from the data of the package `dresscode/upgrade-nette`, each verified by a run of DressCode. The complete list is in the data of the package, one file per library, for example [utils.neon |https://github.com/dg/dresscode-upgrade-nette/blob/master/upgrading/utils.neon].


nette/utils 4
-------------

| old API | new API | since |
|---|---|---|
| `Strings::startsWith($s, 'x')` | `\str_starts_with($s, 'x')` | 4.0 |
| `Strings::normalizeNewLines($s)` | `Strings::unixNewLines($s)` | 4.0 |
| `Image::FIT \| Image::SHRINK_ONLY` | `Image::OrSmaller \| Image::ShrinkOnly` | 4.0 |
| `Json::encode($v, Json::PRETTY)` | `Json::encode($v, pretty: true)` | 4.0 |
| `Arrays::grep($a, $p, PREG_GREP_INVERT)` | `Arrays::grep($a, $p, invert: true)` | 4.0 |
| `Arrays::map($a, callback: $fn)` | `Arrays::map($a, transformer: $fn)` | 4.0.4 |
| `Html::fromHtml($s)` | `Html::html($s)` | 4.1.5 |

The other `Image` constants (`EXACT`, `FILL`, `STRETCH`, `EMPTY_GIF`), `Strings::contains()` and `endsWith()`, and the flags of `Json::decode()`, `Strings::match()`, `matchAll()` and `split()` are rewritten the same way.


nette/php-generator 4
---------------------

| old API | new API | since |
|---|---|---|
| `ClassType::class('Order')` | `new ClassType('Order')` | 4.0.1 |
| `ClassType::VISIBILITY_PUBLIC` | `Visibility::Public` | 4.0.10 |
| `$method->body` | `$method->getBody()` | 4.0 |
| `ClassType::withBodiesFrom($c)` | `ClassType::from($c, withBodies: true)` | 4.0 |

DressCode adds the import of `Nette\PhpGenerator\Visibility` by itself.


nette/mail 4 and nette/robot-loader 4
-------------------------------------

| old API | new API | since |
|---|---|---|
| `Message::HIGH` | `Message::High` | `nette/mail` 4.0 |
| `$mail->subject` | `$mail->getSubject()` | `nette/mail` 4.0 |
| `$loader->setTempDirectory($dir)` | `$loader->setCacheDirectory($dir)` | `nette/robot-loader` 4.1.3 |


What Gets Reported
==================

Where there is no replacement, or a person has to choose it, DressCode reports the place and leaves the code alone. The message says what to write instead:

/--pre .[terminal]
app/Samples.php:30:22: error: Static method `Nette\Utils\Finder::findFiles()` is deprecated: pass the masks as one array, since nette/utils 4.0. [upgrading.api.forbiddenMembers]
app/Samples.php:32:9: error: Static property `Nette\Utils\Html::$xhtml` is removed: there is no replacement; the output is always HTML5; drop the setting, since nette/utils 4.0. [upgrading.api.forbiddenMembers]
\--

| old API | what to write instead | since |
|---|---|---|
| `Finder::findFiles('*.php', '*.phpt')` | the masks as one array, `findFiles(['*.php', '*.phpt'])` | `nette/utils` 4.0 |
| `Html::$xhtml` | nothing, the output is always HTML5; delete the setting | `nette/utils` 4.0 |
| `Image::rgb()` | `ImageColor::rgb()`, which returns an object and takes the opacity as a number from 0 to 1 | `nette/utils` 4.0.3 |
| `Nette\Iterators\Mapper` | `Iterables::map()`, which returns a generator you can iterate only once | `nette/utils` 4.0.5 |
| `ClassType::addExtend()` | `setExtends()`, a class extends at most one class | `nette/php-generator` 4.0.1 |

You confirm such a place with the comment `// dresscode:ignore <decision> -- <reason>`, or rewrite it; [Places Left for You |upgrade#Places Left for You] has the details.


Step by Step
============

DressCode needs `nette/utils` 4.1, so it does not fit into an application on Nette 3 as a development dependency. Install it globally, with PHPStan and the data for Nette:

```shell
composer global require dresscode/dresscode dresscode/upgrade-nette phpstan/phpstan
```

1. Measure how much work the upgrade takes: `dresscode upgrade estimate nette/utils 4.0`. The line `Composer` says whether something in `composer.lock` refuses the target version.
2. Save the plan with the test command, so that the team can review it: `dresscode upgrade plan nette/utils 4.0 --save --test-command "vendor/bin/tester tests -o junit:{junit}"`.
3. Carry it out: `dresscode upgrade run`. The tests run after each step, and a step after which a test newly fails goes back. At the Composer step, DressCode asks whether it may raise `nette/utils` to `^4.0`.
4. Go through what is left for you, and run `upgrade run` again until the run ends with `UPGRADED`.

The other libraries move the same way, only with another target, such as `dresscode upgrade estimate nette/php-generator 4.2`. Without a target, DressCode proposes every library it has newer data about than the project allows today. [Upgrade Your Code Step by Step |upgrade] describes the whole procedure with tests, commits and places left for you.


